# Wazuh SIEM Monitoring on Kali Linux

## Overview
This project demonstrates hands-on Security Operations Center (SOC) monitoring
using *Wazuh SIEM* in a *Kali Linux* environment. The focus is on host-based
log collection, alert analysis, and basic threat hunting activities.

The project simulates how a SOC analyst reviews security events, evaluates alert
severity, and interprets authentication and privilege-related activities.

---

## Objective
- Monitor Linux system activity using Wazuh
- Analyze authentication and session-related logs
- Detect and review privilege escalation events
- Perform alert triage using the Wazuh dashboard
- Understand alert severity and event context

---

## Environment
- *Operating System:* Kali Linux
- *SIEM Platform:* Wazuh
- *Monitoring Type:* Host-based log monitoring
- *Interface:* Wazuh Web Dashboard

---

## Tools & Technologies
- Wazuh SIEM
- Linux (Kali)
- PAM authentication logs
- Syslog analysis
- Threat Hunting dashboard
- MITRE ATT&CK mapping

---

## Activities Performed
- Accessed the Wazuh dashboard and threat-hunting views
- Monitored login session events (open and close)
- Analyzed authentication success events
- Observed privilege escalation activity (sudo usage)
- Reviewed alert levels and timestamps
- Correlated alerts with MITRE ATT&CK techniques

---

## Key Findings
- Authentication-related events were successfully captured and logged
- Privilege escalation attempts via sudo were detected
- Alerts were mostly low to medium severity
- No critical or high-severity incidents were observed
- Dashboard visualizations helped identify event trends

---

## Alert Summary
| Category | Observation |
|--------|------------|
| Total alerts | 24 |
| Critical severity | 0 |
| High severity | 0 |
| Medium severity | Authentication-related activity |
| Low severity | Routine system events |

---

## Analyst Takeaways
- Not all alerts indicate compromise; context is essential
- Authentication logs are valuable for detecting misuse
- SIEM dashboards support efficient alert triage
- Privilege escalation monitoring is critical in Linux environments
- Threat hunting improves visibility into system behavior

---

## Skills Demonstrated
- SIEM monitoring and alert analysis
- Linux log analysis
- Authentication and session monitoring
- Privilege escalation detection
- Threat hunting fundamentals
- SOC-style documentation

